# @PROJECT_NAME@

This is a KuroganeOS `@TEMPLATE@` SDK scaffold. At the current Developer
checkpoint it intentionally builds **only a freestanding object file**. The
system does not yet expose ring-3 startup code, a syscall transport, or an
application linker contract, so this project cannot be linked or run.

The generated capability probe performs real ABI validation and requires these
future runtime features: `@REQUIRED_FEATURE_NAMES@`. It returns
`KU_STATUS_NOT_SUPPORTED` when the supplied kernel ABI descriptor does not
advertise all of them.

Build against a generated SDK sysroot:

```sh
make KUROGANE_SYSROOT=/path/to/kurogane/sysroot
```

The only expected artifact is `build/@PROJECT_NAME@.o`. Do not treat successful
object compilation as evidence that the template can execute on KuroganeOS.
